# Executive Summary

@body

- A short document that summarizes the longer plan for quick review ([similar to an Abstract]{color=red})
- It usually contains a brief statement of the problem, background information, concise analysis and main conclusions.
- Described as the [most important part]{color=red} of a business plan
- [Limited to 1 page]{color=red} like a resume. Too long will turn off investors.
  - Google\: Biotechnology Executive Summary for many examples

=== layout: one-panel
hidden: true

# Executive Summary

@body

- Turn-It-In on Blackboard
- 3 PAGE LIMIT!
  - Page 1\: Cover Page\: company name, company logo, TOC
  - Page 2\: Executive summary
  - Page 3\: References
- If your executive summary is [longer than 1 page, I will grade it as if the second page is missing]{color=red}, i.e., some of your content will be missing.
  - Check format on turnitin AFTER submission, takes about 2 minutes to process
  - [Similarity scores above 10% will lose points]{color=red}
- You do not need my approval to select a topic, just try to address any comments that I sent you.

=== layout: one-panel
hidden: true

# 3 Page Executive Summary

@body

- Page 1
  - Cover Page
  - Company Name
  - Company Logo
  - Table of Contents (optional)

- Page 2
  - Executive Summary
  - Must fit on one page after uploading
  - Similarity scores above 10% will lose points

- Page 3
  - References
  - Include where you got your facts

