# Pre-Recorded Videos

@body

- Pre-Recorded Videos are [ALLOWED]{color=green}
- The must follow all of the guidelines
- You must use your own voice, no playing videos or using AI generated voices
- The runtime is expect to be
  - within 10% of 4 minutes
  - between 3m36s and 4m24s
- Videos can be uploaded to [YouTube]{color=red} or uploaded to [Blackboard]{color=red} under Assignments.
  - Facebook, Quibi, TikTok are not allowed.
- Videos are due [Thursday Oct 17, 2024 before 12PM noon]{color=red} (or Wed night)
  - Dr. Voss plans to download all of the videos (including from YouTube) to his desktop and play them from his computer to avoid internet connectivity issues.
- If you do create a video, you still need to complete the title and references slide in Google Slides, plus provide info on Slide 2 where to watch your video (YouTube, Blackboard).

=== layout: one-panel
hidden: true

# Shark Tank Suggested Format

@body

- 1. Title Slide (required)
- 2. Present a problem
    - not enough light at night
    - people are sick from blah blah
    - ex-boyfriends are evil
- 3. How big is the problem
    - this many people or things are affected
    - there is 100 billion tons of plastic in the ocean
- 4. Present a solution to problem
    - my company is going to solve problem by doing XYZ
- 5. Tell us the science of how your solution works
    - XYZ is an adenovirus gene therapy that gives worms to ex-boyfriends
- 6. Tell us how your solution is better than other competitors
    - the idiots at Baxter cannot solve this problem, because they do not use worms or adenovirus technology. we have the advantage.
- 7. thanks and references used (required)

- [You do not need to follow this format!]{color=red}

=== layout: one-panel
hidden: true

# Questions to Think About

@body

- What is it?
- How does it work?
- When is it used?
- What will it accomplish?
- When should it not be used?

